course: dictionary
lesson: 12049
title: Citations: where words come from
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A citation can be a line of words quoted from a book, speech or writer, copied exactly as it was written. «"Be yourself; everyone else is already taken," wrote Oscar Wilde.» The quotation marks show these are the writer's own words.
explain: In school projects, a citation is a reference that tells the reader exactly where your facts came from: the author, the title, the page or the website. Giving citations shows you are honest and not copying someone else's work.
explain: Citation can also mean an official written praise, such as for brave action, or in the USA a ticket for breaking a rule, like a parking ticket. Context tells you which meaning is right. A firefighter who gets a citation for bravery is being officially thanked, not fined.
fact: A citation shows where words or facts came from.
fact: «Citation» can mean a line quoted from a book, speech or writer.
fact: «Citation» can mean an official written praise, for example for bravery.
fact: In the USA, a «traffic citation» is a ticket for breaking a traffic rule.
fact: Plural: «citations».
exercise: «Her project had six citations at the back, one for every book she used.» What is a citation in this sentence? | A loud shout in class | A ticket for parking | *A reference showing where information came from | A bright drawing of a book
exercise: «The firefighter received a citation for bravery.» What does citation mean here? | A map | *An official written praise | A court order | A line from a poem
exercise: Which citation shows where the words came from? | Blue and green | Loud music | *Author, title, page, website | Two wet dogs ran past
test: Ella wrote, «According to Smith (2019, page 4), plants need light.» What is the citation for? | To show the writer is angry | To make the sentence longer | *To show where the fact came from | To decorate the page
test: A driver in the USA gets a «traffic citation» for speeding. What is it? | A song about cars | A road map | *A ticket for breaking a rule | A prize for driving well
exam: Which use of citation means a reference to a source? | A song's chorus is repeated | A brave firefighter earns a medal | *Notes at the end of a project list each book and page used | A dog gets a bath
